`fetch.ts` `fetchDocument` already returns `{ url, html: "", contentType }` when
`!isHtmlContentType(contentType)` (e.g. `application/pdf`, `application/json`).
But `preview.ts` `extractPreview` treats `html === ""` as an error:
```
if (fetched.html === "") {
  throw new PreviewError("PARSE_ERROR", `No HTML content at ${rawUrl}`, { url });
}
```
Result: a non-HTML URL maps to `PARSE_ERROR` → HTTP 502. The standard requires
an empty-fields result, not an error.

New `packages/core/src/extractors/url.ts`; `extractors/default.ts` (import from
new module); `adapters/youtube.ts`; `adapters/twitter.ts`; `youtube.test.ts`;
`twitter.test.ts`. No server or public-API signature change.

# Adapter Authoring

Adapters provide site-specific extraction (YouTube, Twitter/X, etc.) and plug
into the core adapter registry.

## Interface
```ts
interface AdapterContext {
  url: URL;                 // final, normalized URL
  html: string;             // raw fetched HTML
  $: cheerio.Root;          // parsed Cheerio root (do not re-parse)
}

interface Adapter {
  /** Stable unique id, e.g. "youtube", "twitter", "default". */
  name: string;
  /** Return true if this adapter should handle the URL. Cheap, sync. */
  match(url: URL): boolean;
  /** Extract a result (full or partial). Return null to defer to the next adapter. */
  extract(ctx: AdapterContext): PreviewResult | Partial<PreviewResult> | null;
}
```

## Rules
- **Pure given input:** adapters receive already-fetched HTML + URL. They MUST NOT fetch the network themselves. This keeps them fast, deterministic, and unit-testable offline.
- **Matching is hostname-based** and must be cheap (sync, no I/O). Match on `url.hostname` patterns.
- **Order matters:** the registry is an ordered list; first `match()` wins. Built-ins: `youtube`, `twitter` (X), then `default` (OG extractor) last.
- **Extractors may return partial results** — the engine fills `url`, `fetchedAt`, `fromCache`, `adapter` and backfills missing fields via the default precedence. Set `adapter` implicitly from `name`.
- **Registration:** users add adapters via `preview(url, { adapters: [myAdapter] })` (prepended) or `registerAdapter(myAdapter)`. Prepend custom adapters so they run before built-ins.
- **Built-in adapters** ship in `packages/core/src/adapters/` and are enabled by default. They can be disabled via options.

## Authoring checklist
1. Match on hostname only (no path parsing for `match`; path logic goes in `extract`).
2. Resolve all returned URLs to absolute (use the page base).
3. Handle the page providing nothing → return `null` to defer, never throw.
4. Add a colocated `*.test.ts` using a saved HTML fixture (no network).

