# PreviewResult Output Contract

This is the **stable public contract** for both the library API and the HTTP
server. Changing field names or removing fields is a breaking change.

## TypeScript
```ts
interface PreviewResult {
  /** Final URL after redirects, normalized to a string. Always present. */
  url: string;
  /** Title. Precedence: og:title > twitter:title > <title>. Empty string if none. */
  title: string;
  /** Description. Precedence: og:description > twitter:description > meta description. Empty string if none. */
  description: string;
  /** Primary preview image, if any. Omit the field entirely when absent. */
  image?: PreviewImage;
  /** Site name from og:site_name, if present. */
  siteName?: string;
  /** Adapter that produced this result, e.g. "youtube" or "default". Always present. */
  adapter: string;
  /** Unix epoch milliseconds of the underlying (non-cached) fetch. */
  fetchedAt: number;
  /** True when the result was served from cache. */
  fromCache: boolean;
}

interface PreviewImage {
  url: string;
  alt?: string;
  width?: number;
  height?: number;
}
```

## Rules
- `url`, `title`, `description`, `adapter`, `fetchedAt`, `fromCache` are always present.
- `image`, `siteName` are present only when the page provides them.
- Never return `null` for an optional field — omit it.
- `image.url` must be an absolute URL (resolve relative URLs against the page base).
- Precedence order (Open Graph > Twitter Card > standard meta) is fixed; adapters may override by returning a full `PreviewResult`.

## Error model (companion contract)
Core throws typed errors; the HTTP server maps them to status codes.
```ts
class PreviewError extends Error {
  code: 'INVALID_URL' | 'TIMEOUT' | 'FETCH_ERROR' | 'PARSE_ERROR' | 'TOO_MANY_REDIRECTS';
  url?: string;
  cause?: unknown;
}
```
HTTP mapping: `INVALID_URL` → 400, `TIMEOUT` → 504, `FETCH_ERROR` → 502,
`PARSE_ERROR` → 502, `TOO_MANY_REDIRECTS` → 502.
Body envelope on error: `{ "error": { "code": string, "message": string } }`.

